==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|mergen}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*murganaz}}, from a pre-Germanic *''mr̥kéno'', *''mr̥kóno'', from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*mr̥Hko||to blink, twinkle}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|morgan}} ({{cog|nds|Morgen}} and {{m|nds|Morrn}} or {{m|nds|Morren}}), {{cog|fy|moarn}}, {{cog|nl|morgen}}, {{cog|goh|morgan}} ({{cog|de|Morgen}}), {{cog|non|morghon}} ({{cog|da|morgen}}, {{cog|sv|morgon}}), {{cog|non|morginn}}, {{m|non|morgunn}}; compare also (from a variant Germanic base) {{cog|non|myrginn}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐌿𐍂𐌲𐌹𐌽𐍃}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmorɣen/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# [[morning|Morning]], [[morn]].
#: ''...on '''morgen'''...''
#:: ''...in the '''morning'''...''
# [[morrow|Morrow]]: the [[morning]] of the [[next]] [[day]].
#: ''...tō '''morgen'''...''
#:: ''...'''tomorrow'''...''

